      "content": "thanks for that. it's a lot better than the draft. \n\none thing though, i just checked the dashboard for the audit and the score for this snippet came back way lower than i expected because it's missing a bunch of the keywords the system looks for (like 'endpoint', 'latency', 'request' etc). \n\ncould you try one more version? i really don't want you to just word-stuff or make it sound like a dictionary, but we do need those terms in there so the audit doesn't flag it as \"incomplete.\" can you integrate them more naturally so it sounds like a professional senior writer wrote it, but still hits those required terms?",
